data aws_bahrain_sku_substitution_note: String = "The one place the fixed-SKU rule could not hold, recorded rather than smoothed over: me-south-1 (Bahrain) does not offer m7i.large, so this row carries m6i.large -- a PREVIOUS-generation 2 vCPU / 8 GiB instance. Its 0.1320 USD/hr is therefore NOT directly comparable to the m7i rows above (an older generation usually prices lower for the same vCPU count, so the true m7i-equivalent Bahrain premium would likely be higher still, not lower). Instance-family availability differing by region is itself the finding: newer silicon reaches the largest regions first, so a smaller region pays more AND gets older hardware."

